# Lucid's local settings. Copy this file to .env (`cp .env.example .env`); .env is git-ignored,
# so secrets you put there stay on your machine. Every setting is read from the environment at startup
# (docs/pcr/0001), and the server says on startup which features are on.
#
# Out of the box this runs as the dev user with no outside accounts: start Postgres
# (`docker compose up -d`), run `go run ./cmd/seed` once for made-up deals, then `go run ./cmd/server`.
# The sections after "Server and database" are optional and off until you fill them in.
#
# Never put real company or contact data in a local database (docs/pcr/0007): seed data, and your own
# addresses for testing integrations, only.

# --- Server and database -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bind address. Keep 127.0.0.1 locally: 0.0.0.0 on a machine with a public IP is reachable from the
# internet. The container sets it empty, to bind all interfaces.
HOST=127.0.0.1
# 8000 is growth-portal's and 8001 luma-service's locally. The container listens on 8000.
PORT=8002

# Postgres from `docker compose up -d`.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://crm:crm@127.0.0.1:5436/crm?sslmode=disable

# --- Sign-in: pick one ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A) The dev user (default): every request is signed in as this user, no Google account needed
#    (docs/pcr/0007). `go run ./cmd/seed` makes them an admin. Local only, never in a deployed
#    environment.
DEV_USER_EMAIL=dev@kthais.com

# B) Real Google sign-in (docs/adr/0004). Comment out DEV_USER_EMAIL above (the server refuses both),
#    then:
#    - Use the CRM's Google OAuth client (ask whoever runs the Google Cloud project), and add
#      PUBLIC_URL/auth/callback to its authorized redirect URIs.
#    - PUBLIC_URL is where you open the app: http://127.0.0.1:5174 with `npm run dev`, or
#      http://127.0.0.1:8002 with the frontend built into the server.
#    - Only people on the team get in: appoint yourself first, once, with
#      `go run ./cmd/server appoint-admin you@kthais.com` (docs/adr/0005).
#    OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET is a secret. OIDC_ISSUER and SIGN_IN_DOMAIN below are the defaults: the issuer
#    becomes identity-service's URL once it's live.
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5174
# OIDC_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com
# SIGN_IN_DOMAIN=kthais.com

# --- Connect Gmail (optional; needs B) -----------------------------------------------------------

# Members connect their own mailbox, so emails with contacts land on deals (docs/adr/0006). Needs the
# Gmail API and the gmail.readonly scope on the Google project, and PUBLIC_URL/auth/gmail/callback in
# the client's redirect URIs (see the README's "Connect Gmail").
#
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY, a secret, seals the stored Gmail tokens; setting it turns Connect Gmail on.
# Make one with `openssl rand -base64 32`, and keep it: changing it makes stored connections
# unreadable, so members would connect again.
# TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
#
# Only once sign-in is no longer Google's own client (identity-service): Gmail's own Google client
# (the secret is a secret). Until then Gmail uses the OIDC client above.
# GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Connect Fathom (optional; needs B and TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY) -------------------------------------

# Members connect their own Fathom, so their meetings with contacts land on deals (docs/adr/0008). The
# client ID and secret (a secret) come from Fathom's OAuth app, which Platform registers with
# PUBLIC_URL/auth/fathom/callback; setting both turns Connect Fathom on. Fathom only redirects to
# https and must reach the webhooks, so locally PUBLIC_URL is a tunnel (an ngrok domain registered with
# the app), with that tunnel's callbacks added to the Google client too. With a tunnel open, never set
# DEV_USER_EMAIL: anyone reaching it would be signed in as an admin. See the README's "Connect Fathom".
# FATHOM_CLIENT_ID=
# FATHOM_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Where tokens come from, while it's unclear which of Fathom's two URLs works (the docs' is the default):
# FATHOM_TOKEN_URL=https://fathom.video/external/v1/oauth2/token
